{# The library-API section, shared by every engine template that feeds the #}
{# library/API findings. Parameterized by (findings list, heading text, scan #}
{# coverage record) so each template passes its own heading text and the #}
{# coverage the producing scan stamped. The body is verbatim-pinned by the #}
{# section suite in src/lib.rs — wording or formatting drift fails CI. #}
{# The coverage record (issue #346) arrives as CoverageInfo strings: the #}
{# scan's status word and its admission line. The include appends exactly #}
{# one "Coverage:" qualification line — beside the entries, or as the whole #}
{# section beside the heading when the scan stamped no findings but admits #}
{# falling short — whenever the record carries an admission; a complete or #}
{# missing record renders exactly what it rendered before. #}
{% macro libraries_apis_section(findings, heading, coverage) %}
{% if !findings.is_empty() %}
## {{ heading }}

The following library APIs were identified by static analysis — from the
binary's import table and from the call paths reaching them out of this
function. Where a finding is credible, call the API through the suggested
Rust crate instead of transliterating the raw import or declaring it as an
`extern "C"` stub:

{% for finding in findings %}
- **{{ finding.suggestion|safe }}** for `{{ finding.api }}` ({{ finding.library }} {{ finding.kind }}, confidence {{ finding.confidence }})
{% if !finding.function.is_empty() %}  Reached by: `{{ finding.function }}`
{% endif %}  Evidence: `{{ finding.evidence|safe }}`
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% if !coverage.admission.is_empty() %}
{% if findings.is_empty() %}
## {{ heading }}

{% endif %}
Coverage: {{ coverage.admission }}

{% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
